# Workshop SPA Conventions

## Feature directories and lazy loading

- The package at `crates/workshop/ui/` is a sibling of the `crates/workshop/server/` crate that builds and serves it. `src/` has three layers: `base/` (paths), `services/` (the app's services and their tokens; services own no views), and `parts/` (feature directories; every panel extends `WorkshopPart` from `@workshop/platform/workshop-part`). All three layers may import `@workshop/platform`, the family's UI mechanics (lifecycle, events, the registries, the context-key and text-control services, the `WorkshopPart` base class), which never imports the app.
- Feature-based directories under `parts/` (`parts/agent/`, `parts/chatbox/`, `parts/chrome/`, `parts/editor/`, `parts/gateway/`, `parts/layout/`, `parts/menu/`, `parts/quickinput/`, `parts/run/`, `parts/status/`, `parts/stt/`, `parts/take/`, `parts/workspace/`, `parts/workspace-document/`). Shared code is defined with the entry bundle below; the panel dialog helper lives in `parts/shared/`, and the boot-loaded icons come from `@workshop/look/icons`; per-component tokens live in `tokens/component.css`. The workspace tree panel, its `tree` factory, and its Explorer and Primary Side Bar actions live in `parts/workspace/`; `parts/layout/` holds the layout machinery (zones, boot, persistence, and the keybinding dispatcher), and no `parts/layout` module imports `parts/workspace`.
- A part that the panel registry loads lazily has an `index.ts` as its chunk entry (`crates/workshop/platform/panel-registry.ts`), and other parts need none. Lazy directories export `register()` installing panel factories.
- The entry bundle is the eagerly loaded composition: `crates/workshop/ui/src/main.ts` and the `*.contribution.ts` modules it imports. Lazy panels never import a module inside it, directly or through another import. Everything else that eager and lazy code both import, such as `@workshop/platform`, `services/`, `base/`, and shared parts modules like `parts/layout/zones.ts`, is shared code. Lazy panels load via dynamic `import()` on first activation.
- Registration, not central wiring: panel types, menu items, services, socket handlers, keyboard shortcuts, and lifecycle disposal self-register through the panel, menu/command, and service registries. The menu, command, keybinding, and service registries live in `@workshop/platform`.

## CSS colocation and tokens

- CSS lives beside its TypeScript, imported as a side-effect. Never a separate `styles/` tree. Every feature directory is self-contained: its `.ts` and `.css` sit together, plus an `index.ts` when the panel registry loads it lazily. A designer finds the styles for the agent chat at `parts/agent/agent-session.css`, not by grepping a flat directory.
- No raw color, size, or spacing values in Workshop UI component CSS. The sizes and semantic tiers live in `@workshop/look`: primitives in `look/sizes.css`, intent aliases in `look/semantic.css`. Per-component overrides live in `ui/src/tokens/component.css`. Sizes and elevation are themed in `look/semantic.css`, and colors in `look/tokens.css`, which `look`'s own component sheets read directly.
- CSS classes use the `.ws-` project prefix (`.ws-agent-toolbar`).
- Directories and files are kebab-case (`agent-session-view.ts`, `agent-session.css`).
